From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 06:18:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: defconfig: Enable CPU idle injection cooling

The A733 device tree adds idle injection as the cooling stage between
cpufreq throttling and the critical trip, through thermal-idle nodes in
the CPU nodes. The i.MX8MP, RK3399 and R-Car V4H Sparrow Hawk device
trees have such nodes too, but the arm64 defconfig registers no cooling
device for any of them.

Enable the idle injection framework, the powercap menu it sits in and
the CPU idle cooling device. All three are bool.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: the idle cooling devices of cpu2 to cpu7
registered and the thermal core drove them.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/configs/defconfig | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
index 1ac0dd2f665f..3f73dc0ed104 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
@@ -775,6 +775,7 @@ CONFIG_SENSORS_INA3221=m
 CONFIG_SENSORS_TMP102=m
 CONFIG_THERMAL_GOV_POWER_ALLOCATOR=y
 CONFIG_CPU_THERMAL=y
+CONFIG_CPU_IDLE_THERMAL=y
 CONFIG_DEVFREQ_THERMAL=y
 CONFIG_THERMAL_EMULATION=y
 CONFIG_IMX_SC_THERMAL=m
@@ -1815,6 +1816,8 @@ CONFIG_PHY_AM654_SERDES=m
 CONFIG_PHY_J721E_WIZ=m
 CONFIG_OMAP_USB2=m
 CONFIG_PHY_XILINX_ZYNQMP=m
+CONFIG_POWERCAP=y
+CONFIG_IDLE_INJECT=y
 CONFIG_ARM_CCI_PMU=m
 CONFIG_ARM_CCN=m
 CONFIG_ARM_CMN=m
